config AL_ETH
	bool "Annapurna Labs al_eth (Alpine V2 / AL-324) Ethernet"
	depends on DM_ETH
	select PHYLIB
	help
	  DM_ETH driver for the Alpine V2 integrated Ethernet MAC. The 1G RGMII
	  port (UNVR eth1 @ PCI 1c36:0001, AR8033 PHY on MDIO addr 4) is always
	  built; AL_ETH_10G adds the SFP+ port.

	  The Annapurna HAL is NOT bundled here. It is staged at build time from
	  modules/al_eth/ - the single source shared with the Linux driver - so a
	  fix landed there is a fix here too (#256).

config AL_ETH_DEBUG
	bool "al_eth + al_serdes verbose HAL trace (-DDEBUG)"
	depends on AL_ETH
	help
	  Compile the al_eth and al_serdes directories with -DDEBUG, which turns
	  every HAL al_dbg() and driver debug()/dev_dbg() into a console print:
	  the full UDMA descriptor-fetch and adapter bring-up trace, plus every
	  SerDes PMA register access. Thousands of lines per boot.

	  Off by default. `eth diag` answers the usual "why is this port down"
	  question on demand; turn this on only to trace a bring-up live - e.g.
	  the last register logged before an SError names the faulting access.

config AL_ETH_10G
	bool "Annapurna Labs al_eth 10G SFP+ (eth2, 1c36:0002)"
	depends on AL_ETH
	select AL_SERDES
	help
	  DM_ETH driver for the 10G SFP+ port (UNVR eth2, PCI 1c36:0002) in
	  AL_ETH_MAC_MODE_10GbE_Serial (fixed 10.3125 Gbps, KR AN/LT off). Shares
	  the whole UDMA/EC datapath with the 1G port; adds only the SerDes lane
	  (via CONFIG_AL_SERDES) and the no-PHY PCS-block-lock link gate.
